  "caption": "Sometimes…there’s nothing you can do! I like to think of negativity as fuel to keep you going. And if you’re receiving it, it probably means you’re getting far along just fine, don’t let it change your route, but acknowledge the privilege…see you around for more stories",
  "transcript": {
    "text": "There is nothing you can do to make them like you. I used to want to please the world until I realized what made them happy, made me sad, and that's an unnegotiable. I see it's probably easier to not like me because I represent myself unapologetically. I used to hate people like that, that is until I realized they just didn't get it. You know how long it takes to like somebody? Like really like somebody? If you're anything like me, it probably takes a while. I wouldn't want anyone to like me if their distance to dislike me is shorter. I'll see you around for more stories.",
